  {
   "id": "ded_table",
   "fact": "Dedicated switch table 0x040f4074: 32 records x 32 B (table of tables entry 0x36dd4). ROM switch number of Dn = 128 + n (dispatcher loop 0x81..0xa0). Rows: dedicated_switches.csv",
   "value": {
    "ptr": "0x40f4074",
    "count": 32,
    "record_size": 32,
    "tot_addr": "0x36dd4"
   },
   "address": "0x040f4074, 0x36dd4",
   "tag": "code",
   "evidence": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "ded_22_23",
   "fact": "D22 = MINUS, D23 = PLUS. Evidence: (1) ROM names in the table; (2) the shared handler 0xfea8 passes mask 2 for D22 and 4 for D23 to 0xfc20, and the service code uses mask 2 to move back / volume down, 4 forward / up; (3) PinMAME's input port maps key 8 'Minus' to bit 0x200 (D22) and key 9 'Plus' to 0x400 (D23); (4) emulator: key 8 -> 0xfc20(r0 = 0x96 = switch 150 = D22, mask 2), key 9 -> 0x97 (151, D23, mask 4). Only the comment block in PinMAME sam.c ('D21 - DED #22 - Plus, D22 - DED #23 - Minus') says otherwise; it is wrong",
